      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Patrick Michaud will talk about the &lt;a href=&#34;http://dev.perl.org/perl6/&#34;&gt;Perl 6 programming language&lt;/a&gt; from a variety of perspectives, and targeting a number of different audiences.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Patrick will look at some of the changes and improvements that &lt;a href=&#34;http://dev.perl.org/perl6/&#34;&gt;Perl 6&lt;/a&gt; has made as a language over previous versions of Perl, as well as many of the technical details of its implementation. &#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Along the way he&amp;#39;ll also take a look at &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.parrotcode.org/&#34;&gt;Parrot&lt;/a&gt;, and see how it is progressing to become a common runtime platform for Perl, Python, PHP, Ruby, Javascript, and many other dynamic languages.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
